<title>SINGAPORE: Asiamatrix first-half net loss narrows.</title>
<headline>Asiamatrix first-half net loss narrows.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net loss				1.34   vs   2.49</p>
<p>    Loss per share (cents)	    5.34   vs  11.09</p>
<p>    Turnover				3.57   vs   3.43</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		  0.31   vs   0.29</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortization	 0.80   vs   0.98</p>
<p>    Pre-tax loss			  1.34   vs   2.49</p>
<p>    Tax					nil   vs    nil</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries	    (gain) 0.52   vs    nil</p>
<p>Note - Electronics company Asiamatrix Ltd said losses declined in the first half due to better human resource management, control of operating costs and a write-back of a provision for doubtful debts of Singapore $265,000.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
